===Etymology===
{{inh+|en|enm|enheritaunce}}, {{m|enm|inheritaunce}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|-}}, {{der|en|fro|enheritaunce}}, from {{m|fro|enheriter}}.
Equivalent to {{suf|en|inherit|ance}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈhɛɹɪtəns/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-inheritance.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The passing of [[title]] to an [[estate]] upon death.
# {{lb|en|countable}} That which a person is entitled to [[inherit]], by law or [[testament]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable|especially|linguistics|biology}} The act or mechanism of inheriting; the state of having inherited.
#: {{ux|en|The Indo-European languages share various similarities as a result of their '''inheritance''' from a common ancestor.}}
# {{lb|en|biology|[[w:genetic algorithm|genetic algorithm]]s}} The biological [[attribute]]s passed [[hereditarily]] from ancestors to their [[offspring]].
# {{lb|en|programming|object-oriented}} The mechanism whereby parts of a [[superclass]] are available to instances of its [[subclass]].

